WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:05.280
There's a very interesting development, which
is that Donald Trump has a serious primary

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:06.280
challenger.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:08.000
Now, let me sort of [inaudible] explain

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:09.250
what I mean by serious.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.490
By serious, I don't mean someone that has
any chance of actually beating Donald Trump

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:19.950
in the republican primary, but it's serious
in that it's someone who is more of an actual

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:26.070
republican as far as the perception of him
than William Weld who's running against Trump,

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.210
and his name is Joe Walsh.

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.449
He's a former congressman.

00:00:29.449 --> 00:00:34.010
Joe Walsh told George Stephanopoulos on his
ABC Sunday morning show yesterday that he

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:38.290
is running for president and the Republican
primary against Donald Trump.

00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:42.980
President points too often is just about every
poll shows more than 80% support for the president

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:44.210
among Republicans.

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:45.320
They don't have an alternative.

00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:51.130
I'll tell you what, George [inaudible] look,
I'm running because he's unfair.

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:55.510
Somebody needs to step up and there needs
to be an alternative.

00:00:55.510 --> 00:00:59.420
The country is sick of this guy's Tantrum.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:01.010
He's, he's a child.

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:04.819
Again, the litany he lies every time he opens
his mouth.

00:01:04.819 --> 00:01:07.670
Now everything is working against this guy.

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:12.690
Okay? Trump has a very high approval rating
among Republicans, but not as high as Trump

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:13.690
thinks.

00:01:13.690 --> 00:01:15.259
Trump says it's a 95% approval rating.

00:01:15.259 --> 00:01:16.259
It's more like 80.

00:01:16.259 --> 00:01:18.880
According to a new, uh, Associated Press poll.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:25.540
Walsh has a lot of exploitable personal issues,
including allegedly being a deadbeat dad.

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:30.490
The Republican National Committee isn't going
to support a primary challenge to Donald Trump,

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:34.899
but, and this is the dream, Joe Walsh might
be able to get in the way just enough to become

00:01:34.899 --> 00:01:37.529
an annoyance to Donald Trump, which would
be really great.

00:01:37.529 --> 00:01:41.639
Trump has a high approval rating among Republicans,
but it's not set in stone.

00:01:41.639 --> 00:01:46.060
Many republicans say they support Trump merely
because they don't like Democrats and it's

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:48.039
their way of showing it.

00:01:48.039 --> 00:01:54.419
But there is 21% of Republicans that already
does not support Donald Trump, and that is

00:01:54.419 --> 00:02:02.399
a, a fifth of the party that might be interested
in an alternative Republican to Donald Trump.

00:02:02.399 --> 00:02:07.289
The RNC won't support a primary challenge,
but they don't even really need to because

00:02:07.289 --> 00:02:11.269
the goal here is not to beat Trump in the
primary.

00:02:11.269 --> 00:02:16.530
In the same way that the goal of an impeachment
inquiry isn't to remove Trump before 2020

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.790
the goal of all of these ideas is to weaken
Donald Trump.

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:24.700
So do we on the left want people running against
Trump from within the Republican party?

00:02:24.700 --> 00:02:25.700
Absolutely.

00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:29.239
The stronger they are, the happier we are
to see it.

00:02:29.239 --> 00:02:33.500
Democrats can just keep running their primary
and meanwhile, anything that could weaken

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.040
Donald Trump is a good thing.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:41.480
Walsh running against Trump might lead to
some money being spent that otherwise wouldn't,

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:48.459
and impeachment inquiry would replace some
Trump campaign media stories with some impeachment

00:02:48.459 --> 00:02:51.150
inquiry stories and that could damage Donald
Trump.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:55.670
Remember 2016 was decided by 70,000 votes
in three states.

00:02:55.670 --> 00:02:59.200
Any of these things that could weaken Donald
Trump or interfere with Donald Trump being

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.390
able to set the narrative, we should welcome
and we should encourage.

00:03:03.390 --> 00:03:05.469
This is Donald Trump's strength.

00:03:05.469 --> 00:03:11.109
When he sets the narrative and gets the media
in a frenzy, gets them spending three, five

00:03:11.109 --> 00:03:16.439
or seven days on something that Trump benefits
from, or at least that Trump would prefer

00:03:16.439 --> 00:03:22.330
they focus on other than some more damaging
thing that is good for Donald Trump.

00:03:22.330 --> 00:03:26.250
Joe Walsh is a disgusting ideological clown.

00:03:26.250 --> 00:03:30.469
He's completely unqualified to be president
of the United States, but Republicans already

00:03:30.469 --> 00:03:33.200
voted in a guy who's completely unqualified
to be president.

00:03:33.200 --> 00:03:34.650
By all means have at it.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:36.519
Joe, see what you can do.

00:03:36.519 --> 00:03:39.400
See what amount of support he can pick off
from the Republican Party.

00:03:39.400 --> 00:03:45.700
And by the way, don't forget, and this is
like the dream scenario, if Joe Walsh can

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:51.870
get some traction with the fifth of the Republican
Party that doesn't approve of Trump, again,

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:56.800
latest poll from the Associated Press, 79%
of Republicans approve of Trump.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:57.800
21% don't.

00:03:57.800 --> 00:04:00.519
Okay, that's one fifth of Republicans.

00:04:00.519 --> 00:04:07.999
If Joe Walsh can pick up 3% support, 5% support
in the Republican primary, obviously he loses

00:04:07.999 --> 00:04:09.689
the primary.

00:04:09.689 --> 00:04:10.900
That may be enough.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:15.640
It may give them enough money and may give
them enough momentum to say, you know what,

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:17.099
I'm going to run as a third party.

00:04:17.099 --> 00:04:22.889
Because Joe Walsh has said he's a terrible
guy, but he said he apologizes for his role

00:04:22.889 --> 00:04:25.390
in helping to elect Trump in 2016.

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:30.280
If his goal is really to do anything he can
to remove Trump, he might say, I'm going to

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:31.699
run third party.

00:04:31.699 --> 00:04:37.490
And they're, when you look at how close it
was in so many key states, Wisconsin, Michigan,

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:43.770
other states, Joe Walsh running as a Republican
could actually, I'm sorry, Joe Walsh running

00:04:43.770 --> 00:04:48.470
as an independent could actually take enough
Republican votes away from Donald Trump that

00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:53.510
it flips one state to the eventual Democratic
nominee, two states to the eventual democratic

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:54.510
nominee.

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:56.300
So this is not strategy for the left.

00:04:56.300 --> 00:05:00.960
What we need to do is run a fair primary,
uh, and then get people to vote, get people

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.190
to vote who otherwise wouldn't.

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:03.360
Half the country doesn't vote.

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:04.920
Find people who already agree with us.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:09.979
Tell them this was a very small margin in
this state and that state in whichever state

00:05:09.979 --> 00:05:10.979
you should vote.

00:05:10.979 --> 00:05:12.870
That's still our strategy.

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:17.610
But if Joe Walsh is going to create an annoying
distraction, like a mosquito that you just

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:23.430
can't get to get, leave you alone for Donald
Trump up until the republican national convention

00:05:23.430 --> 00:05:29.720
and then might actually run as an independent,
he could single handedly hand a state or two

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:33.740
to the Democratic nominee and conceivably
turn this election.

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:34.830
It might not happen.

00:05:34.830 --> 00:05:39.440
We should support it because it does nothing
bad for us and potentially does some good

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:40.440
things.

00:05:40.440 --> 00:05:41.440
Yeah.

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:45.990
Uh, it's, it's an obvious dead end in what
it is in that Trump is going to be the Republican

00:05:45.990 --> 00:05:48.220
nominee unless he were to drop out or something.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:49.220
Who knows.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:54.160
Uh, but it is not a dead end in that it could
have a real impact and really hurt Donald

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:56.160
Trump in the eventual general election.

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:00.680
If you disagree with me, tell me where I'm
wrong on the numbers.

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:01.680
Okay.

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:05.500
Uh, if you disagree with me for some other
reason, I guess also let me know, but the

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:09.000
real case I'm making is that mathematically
this could have an impact that is not good

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:09.010
for Donald Trump.

